    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1028">

                <pb facs="1186" n="1074" xml:id="pg1074"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.628/108: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-03-08T18:00:00-05:00">March 8, 1935—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. Department’s instructions No. 639, November 19, 1934. We would appreciate
                    receipt as soon as practicable of expression of your views.<anchor n="57"
                        xml:id="d1028-f1"/></p>
                <p>An official of the Bureau of Marine Products, Japanese Department of Agriculture
                    and Forestry, who is now in the United States, manifested to an officer of the
                    Department and to an officer of the Bureau of Fisheries interest in the
                    possibility of revision of the Fur Seals Treaty.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d1028-f2"
                    /> Have there been indications of a revival of interest in Japan in this
                        matter?<anchor n="59" xml:id="d1028-f3"/></p>
                <p>Please refrain from consulting Japanese officials in connection with either of
                    these matters.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1028-f1" n="57" xml:id="d1028-f1-content">
                <p>The Ambassador’s reply, telegram No. 51, March 9, 1 p.m., suggested “delay
                    pending Russo-Japanese fishery discussions.” (894.628/121)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1028-f2" n="58" xml:id="d1028-f2-content">
                <p>Convention between the United States, the United Kingdom, Japan, and Russia for
                    the preservation and protection of fur seals, signed July 7, 1911, <ref
                        target="frus1911#pg_260"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>,
                        1911, p. 260</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1028-f3" n="59" xml:id="d1028-f3-content">
                <p>For previous correspondence, see <ref target="frus1928v03#pg_147"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1928, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 147</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
